Archives

A Plug-In for Mill. Put it in the "Mill Plug-Ins" folder.

  zip         .zip, stored and deflated members
  tar         .tar, ustar and V7
  gzip        .gz and .tgz
  MacBinary   .bin, I, II, and III
  BinHex      .hqx, 4.0

A link to an archive brings up Mill's dialog: Cancel, Browse, or Save...
Browse lists the members, and a member opens like any page or file, at
an address with "#/" and its name: kit.zip#/docs/readme.txt.

zip and tar are read by parts, so they browse from this Mac's disks and
from servers that can send parts; elsewhere they browse once saved.
gzip, MacBinary, and BinHex browse from anywhere. Saving a member of a
MacBinary or BinHex file makes the Mac file, both forks. A Mac text file
shows in Mac Roman. zip and gzip use Mill's own decompression.

Written from the published specifications (PKWARE's APPNOTE.TXT, POSIX
1003.1-1990 for ustar, RFC 1951 and 1952, the MacBinary II and III
standards, and BinHex 4.0's own notes).

Build: ./build.sh writes build/Archives.bin.
